  nonce: 08cb  # 08cb
  message: "Finalize-stage internal-API co-design PRODUCED and RATIFIED (open decision #4), documented as ADR-0043 §6.1 (PR #230, dev 7f8e72a22e). The single finalize stage's internal API is now specified: an explicit-body finalize(ctx)->frozen FinalizedMap orchestrator (source order = schedule) with house-style _finalize_<concern>(ctx)->None sub-steps and two white-box guard tests (R2 recompute-after-stamp / META-hufaz; R3 FK-check-last / §7); a Protocol/toposort was rejected as over-engineering for the closed ~four-edge DAG. The 10-substep order, dependency rules R1-R8, PYTHONHASHSEED-independence (in the re_derive_view projection-consumer helper), and the four ratified sub-decisions (config_fingerprint backstop-with-violation; emission-counts per-run-by-origin_run_id; shallow frozen FinalizedMap; amendment-not-new-ADR) are all in §6.1. This DESIGN-unblocks run-lifecycle:F1 (the carrier) + META-hufaz + WI-mipul, which were blocked on this co-design. NOTE: run-lifecycle:F1 remains SEQUENCING-gated per ADR-0043 §Sequencing-constraint — it lands only AFTER the identity-v6 / py.py scope-stack rewrite (seam b) and the WI-pozur Phase D/E reorder (seam a), so the substrate is final on finalize() entry. Phasing: F1 carrier lands the module + spine + run-lifecycle sub-steps with the other 3 families (projection-finalize, declared-fields, confidence) as documented stubs filling named slots later. META-jalur closure is unchanged (§8 serialization round-trip property test, lands with the implementing fixes). Working artifact: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/finalize_stage_codesign_06132026.md."  # 08cb
